# ── The migration workspace. NEVER commit this. ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Decompiling a mod puts somebody else's source on disk. `MIGRATE_WORKSPACE` defaults OUTSIDE any
# repository precisely so this cannot happen, and these entries are the second line of defence for
# anyone who overrides it to a path inside the checkout.
work/
workspace/
decompiled/
decompiled-raw/
original/
mods/
releases/
installs/
out/

# ── Machine-local configuration ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env.local
.setup-state.json
.env.local.bak

# ── Build + tooling output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.gradle/
build/
bin/
run/
*.log

# ── Things that are never ours to publish ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.jar
*.class
# ...except Gradle's own wrapper, which the scaffolds need. It is still allowlisted BY SHA1 in
# tools/check-no-ip.py, so un-ignoring the path does not let a different jar through under this name.
!**/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar

# ── Derived from Mojang's mapping data: generated per user, never published ─────────────────────
# (plan decision 2: ship the generators, not their output)
*2official-*.json
moves-*.tsv
moves-*.ambiguous.txt
moves-*.removed.txt
